        {
          "id": 6351091617,
          "url": "https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor/issues/5957#issuecomment-6351091617",
          "author": "Paraphern",
          "body": "This is a declared-vs-actual contract break, and it's worth fixing as such: the discovery document is a machine-read contract (\"these auth methods are supported\"), and a client that trusts it fails at runtime. The mechanical guard on Casdoor's side: a conformance check in CI that exercises every method advertised in `token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported` — advertised-but-broken then becomes a red build, not a ChatGPT-connector mystery. (We chase the same class on the MCP side: launch selectors and declared capabilities that can't actually resolve are findings at check time, not at first client failure.)\n",
